---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Notice"
  description="How Komadrona Review handles browser progress, hosting logs, external Google Forms, and voluntary contact."
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Version 1 privacy</span>
      <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
      <p>Version 1 is designed to avoid creating a centralized learner profile or database.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <article class="container prose">
    <div class="notice">
      <strong>Progress is local and recoverability is limited</strong>
      <p>
        Completed topics, bookmarks, acknowledgments, and self-recorded scores are stored in this browser. Clearing
        site data or browser storage, using private browsing, reinstalling the browser, changing browsers, or moving
        to another device may permanently reset them. Komadrona Review has no server backup and cannot restore them.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>What the website does not request</h2>
    <p>Komadrona Review Version 1 does not provide accounts and does not ask the website user to submit:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>a name, school, student number, professional license number, phone number, or home address;</li>
      <li>an email address for access to the reviewer;</li>
      <li>a quiz screenshot, score report, identification document, or educational record; or</li>
      <li>health information or patient information.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Information stored in the browser</h2>
    <p>
      The site may use browser local storage for the legal-notice acknowledgment, topic completion, bookmarks, and
      scores that the user records manually. This information is intended to remain on the device and is not designed
      to be transmitted to a Komadrona Review learner database.
    </p>
    <p>
      Browser storage can be inspected, changed, or deleted by a person with access to the device. It should not be
      treated as a secure record, an official grade, or proof of examination readiness.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting and technical records</h2>
    <p>
      The site is planned for static hosting through Vercel. Like ordinary hosting providers, Vercel may process
      technical request, network, security, and diagnostic information needed to deliver and protect the service.
      Komadrona Review does not control the provider's independent processing and does not use those records to build
      learner profiles.
    </p>

    <h2>Google Forms practice quizzes</h2>
    <p>
      Practice quizzes open on Google Forms as an external service rather than inside the website. Version 1 forms are
      intended to avoid questions requesting names and email addresses, and they should not require score screenshots
      to be sent to the maintainer.
    </p>
    <p>
      Google may process technical, cookie, browser, or account information under its own terms and privacy practices,
      including when a user is already signed in to a Google account. Komadrona Review cannot control or erase data
      held independently by Google.
    </p>

    <h2>Voluntary communication</h2>
    <p>
      When a user voluntarily contacts the maintainer to report an error, copyright concern, security problem, or
      source suggestion, the maintainer receives the contact details and message supplied by that user. Such messages
      should not include patient information, examination leaks, government identifiers, or unnecessary personal data.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics, advertising, and tracking</h2>
    <p>
      Version 1 does not intentionally include Google Analytics, Meta Pixel, advertising trackers, behavioral
      profiling tools, or embedded social-media widgets. A later change that introduces analytics or centralized data
      collection must first update this notice and the project's technical documentation.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy principles</h2>
    <p>
      Where personal information is processed through voluntary communication or future features, the project intends
      to apply transparency, a specified legitimate purpose, proportionality, data minimization, reasonable security,
      and limited retention consistent with applicable Philippine privacy requirements.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions and corrections</h2>
    <p>
      A dedicated project contact address will be published before public release. Until then, privacy concerns may be
      raised through the repository's GitHub issue process without posting sensitive personal information publicly.
    </p>

    <p class="small-print">Effective date: 3 August 2026. Applies to Komadrona Review Version 1.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
